 ### Hierarchical Rectilinear Grid (Octree)
-A hierarchical extension using an octree data structure for the interpolated volume to avoid problems of interpolating from curvilinear volumes with irregular sampling densities [S2]. It creates the octree by adding sample points from the original curvilinear grid one by one to the (originally empty) octree. Whenever a particular partition of the octree contains more than a user-specified number of curvilinear data samples, split that node into eight subnodes. After all curvilinear samples are added, calculate the estimated data value at the eight corners of each octree partition. Render the resulting volume using a hierarchical volume ray-tracer or the coherent projection approach. To avoid interpolation errors in creating the octree, an alternative is to use the octree together with the original curvilinear volume and render using values from the original sample values [S2].
